  "question": {
    "text": "The integrating factor of the differential equation $x \\log x \\frac{d y}{d x}+y=2 \\log x$ is given by",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XajWL",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Uiln8",
      "text": "$\\log x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "susnD",
      "text": "$\\log (\\log \\mathrm{x})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "liJwz",
      "text": "$x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $\\frac{d y}{d x}+\\frac{1}{x \\log x} \\cdot y=\\frac{2}{x}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { If }=e^{\\int \\frac{1}{x \\log x} d x}=e^{\\int \\frac{1 / x}{\\log x} d x} \\\\\n& =e^{\\log (\\log x)}=\\log x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
